# Written by lib/check.py on every run: the raw status codes, SQLSTATEs and
# row counts behind each verdict. Useful while debugging a project, and not
# something to commit — it is an OUTPUT of the corpus, and a stale copy in the
# tree would read as evidence for claims nobody re-ran.
evidence.jsonl
# Minted at verify time, never committed. See verify.sh.
*.jwt
